Algorithm: 

step-1:Traverse the 2D grid a perform BFS traversal from each of the cells containing 1. 
step-2:Mark the current cell as visited by changing cell value to 0. 
step-3:The area of the island starting from the current cell is 1. 
step-4:Iteratively visit all the neighbors (up-right-down-left) of current cells that contain 1, 
mark these neighbors as visited, and also increase the area by 1 for every valid neighbor 
 (cells with value 1) visited(by changing cell value to 0). 
step-5:After traversal is complete return the area obtained. 
step-6:Perform steps 2,3,4 and 5 for each of the cells (of the matrix) containing 1 and return a 
maximum of all the area values obtained. 

Procedure: 
we start from the left-most and top-most cell of the largest island that has value 1 
(by now, all the cells above and left of this cell have already been visited) and perform BFS 
traversal. 

BFS traversal first visits all the neighbor cells (up-right-down-left) of a particular cell and 
then iteratively visits neighbors of these neighbors. 

